#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""simulation.py - B3 native task: Ising quench dynamics + diagnostics.

Pipeline:
    1. Load data/parameters.json and data/initial_state.npy.
    2. Run single-spin-flip Metropolis Monte Carlo on a 100x100 Ising lattice
       with periodic boundaries, at temperature T = control (= 2.0236) in J/k_B
       units (below the 2D Ising critical point T_c ~ 2.269).
    3. Collect observables at the times defined by measurement_times
       (energy, |m|, low-k structure-factor magnitudes) and at snapshot_times
       (radial pair correlation, 1D marginals, snapshots for the figure).
    4. Post-process: derive self-similar collapse diagnostics and a power-law
       growth-exponent fit from the saved correlation profiles.
    5. Emit all eight strict output artifacts
       (seriesA/B.npy, stackC/D/E.npy, metadataA/B.json, figure.png).

Reproducibility: only data/initial_state.npy and dynamics_seed are used; the
RNG trajectory is identical on every run.
"""
